    <item>
      <title>Long-Term Partnership and Technological Progress in Precision Grinding</title>
      <link>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-ccm-comork/en/news/comork16/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-ccm-comork/en/news/comork16/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Enduring Partnership and Advancements in Grinding Technology 
    &lt;div id=&#34;enduring-partnership-and-advancements-in-grinding-technology&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#enduring-partnership-and-advancements-in-grinding-technology&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div id=&#34;gallery-f0febcd9857dae581b32b8da0a7ab702&#34; class=&#34;gallery&#34;&gt;
  
  
    
    
&lt;figure class=&#34;grid-w50 pb-4 text-center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://mis3085.github.io/docs-ccm-comork/20210303_news03_1_pic_11610082271122351540.png&#34; alt=&#34;16 Years’ Cooperation Between AUTO STRONG and CCM, Designating the Use of COMORK Machinery&#34; class=&#34;mx-auto max-w-full h-auto&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;16 Years’ Cooperation Between AUTO STRONG and CCM, Designating the Use of COMORK Machinery&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;figure class=&#34;grid-w50 pb-4 text-center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://mis3085.github.io/docs-ccm-comork/20210303_news03_2.jpg-eajedang6h_10326891090827496377.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Ko-Yen General Manager Quan-ji Zhou (left) visits AUTO STRONG’s Vice General Manager Ming-Hsiung Chang (right)&#34; class=&#34;mx-auto max-w-full h-auto&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Ko-Yen General Manager Quan-ji Zhou (left) visits AUTO STRONG’s Vice General Manager Ming-Hsiung Chang (right)&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In 2015, at the Taipei International Machine Tool Show (TIMTOS), Ko-Yen made a significant impression by displaying a red banner that read: “Subverting tradition: One-time processing for multiple-side shaping processing, increasing performance by 50%.” This bold statement was backed by the successful sale of the GJ-400 model showcased at the event, generating considerable momentum for the company.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
